---
description: Tessera operating rules — read before writing any code
alwaysApply: true
---

You are implementing Tessera, a professional product. You are not prototyping.

1. Read `AGENTS.md`, then `docs/18-implementation-playbook.md`, then your ticket in `docs/tasks/`.
2. The spec wins over the ticket. Record disagreements in `docs/questions.md`.
3. Language is TypeScript (strict) except Tauri Rust, TSL/WGSL, and `bridges/*`. Do not reopen ADR-0001.
4. One ticket per PR. Stay inside the ticket `Touches` list. Tests first. Never skip gates.
5. No `any`, `as` (except `as const`), `!`, `@ts-ignore`, `console.*`, default exports, or direct Yjs mutation outside `@tessera/core`.
6. Layer 0–2 returns `Result`. Document mutations go only through the command bus.
7. Use glossary words: document / entity / component / scene / Object3D.
8. If the spec is silent: smallest change that preserves invariants. Do not invent product behavior.
